{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>תבוא</b> — He returns to the soul of the rich man, as written above." "<b>עד דור אבותיו</b> — For they were like him, without wisdom." "<b>עד נצח לא יראו אור</b> — This is the reward and delight of the soul, to light in the light of its master [Adonai], who gave it and He takes it [back]. And thus in the book of Ben Gurion, [one] calls the world to come \"the great light,\" and I have already mentioned its reason."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {2 "I read אדוניה as 'its master' (i.e., the soul's master, Adonai); the phrase שנתנה והוא לקחה echoes Ecclesiastes 12:7, 'who gave it' (the spirit) and 'He takes it' (back)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:22.210951627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}